course: dictionary
lesson: 14352
title: Olfaction: the sense of smell
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your senses tell your brain about the world. You have five: sight, hearing, touch, taste and smell. Olfaction is the scientific word for smell, and it can also mean the act of smelling.
explain: Smell starts in your nose. Tiny particles in the air float in, reach special smell sensors high inside your nose, and send messages to your brain. «I can smell fresh bread from the kitchen» uses your olfaction, even though you never have to think about it.
explain: Olfaction and taste work together. «My nose was blocked, so my apple tasted of almost nothing» shows this: without smell, food tastes much duller. Try holding your nose while you eat a jelly bean and see what happens.
fact: Olfaction means the sense of smell, or the act of smelling.
fact: Olfaction is a biology word, so you will meet it in science lessons.
fact: Smell works when tiny particles in the air reach the sensors in your nose.
fact: Dogs, sharks and bears have much stronger olfaction than humans.
fact: When your nose is blocked, food tastes of less.
exercise: What does olfaction mean? | *The sense of smell | The taste of food | Feeling things with your hands | Hearing sounds from far away
exercise: «The dog used its strong olfaction to find the lost ball.» Which sense did the dog use? | Hearing | Touch | *Smell | Sight
exercise: Which animals have much stronger olfaction than humans? | Only people with a cold | Birds that cannot fly | *Sharks and bears | Goldfish and snails
test: «When my nose was blocked, my soup tasted of almost nothing.» Why? | Soup has no flavour at all | My tongue was too tired | Soup is always bland | *Smell helps us taste food
test: Olfaction works when what reaches your nose? | Bright light | *Tiny particles in the air | Large rocks | Loud sounds
exam: Which sentence about olfaction is true? | Olfaction is only used by fish | Olfaction is the sense of hearing | *Olfaction works when tiny particles in the air reach your nose | Olfaction makes your eyes water
